<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>
  <!--
    What's New module strings (src/Shell/Screens/WhatsNewState.cs + WhatsNewCatalog.cs). The mod keeps a
    record of announcements, one per released version (see WhatsNewCatalog, newest first). When
    the player has unread announcements (e.g. after an update) they are surfaced on the main menu,
    shown one at a time as a buffer the player arrows through line by line.

    Per-version messages are keyed by version with dots replaced by underscores, e.g.
    RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Message.2_0_0 for version 2.0.0. When a version has no message of its
    own, RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Message.Default is shown instead. Paragraphs are separated by
    "\n"; each becomes one line the player arrows to.

    When cutting a release, add a new Message.<version> block here (and translate it in the other
    language folders) and add the version to WhatsNewCatalog. The message is player-facing prose,
    not a raw changelog dump — the full changelog lives on the website, one button-press away.
  -->

  <!-- Header (the first line of each announcement). Header is used when there is more than one
       announcement: {0} = version, {1} = this announcement's number, {2} = total. HeaderSingle is
       used for a lone announcement (the normal case): {0} = version. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Header>RimWorld Access {0}. Announcement {1} of {2}.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Header>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.HeaderSingle>RimWorld Access {0}.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.HeaderSingle>

  <!-- Per-version messages. Paragraphs separated by "\n".
       DRAFT: this 2.0.0 welcome is a working draft; rewrite it in your own words before release,
       then it (and any future announcements) get translated into the other languages. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Message.2_0_0>Welcome to What's New! This message appears whenever RimWorld Access updates, to tell you what changed.\n
RimWorld Access is now version 2.0.0, the first release under new ownership. Thank you for playing, and for helping make RimWorld playable for blind and visually impaired gamers.\n
For the full, detailed changelog, choose Open Changelog to read it on the website.\n
You can reopen this any time from What's New in the main menu or the pause menu. If you would rather not see these appear on their own, choose Don't show these again; you will still hear a brief notice when the mod updates.\n
Press Escape, or choose Close, when you are done. Thanks again, and enjoy!</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Message.2_0_0>

  <!-- Fallback message when a version has no message of its own. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Message.Default>RimWorld Access has been updated. Choose Open Changelog to read what changed on the website.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Message.Default>

  <!-- Buttons reached by arrowing past the last line of the message. -->
  <!-- {0} = number of announcements still unread. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.NextAnnouncement>Jump to next announcement ({0} remaining)</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.NextAnnouncement>
  <!-- {0} = total number of announcements in the record (always 2 or more when this button shows). -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.MarkAllRead>Mark all {0} announcements as read</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.MarkAllRead>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.OpenChangelog>Open changelog in browser</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.OpenChangelog>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.Close>Close</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.Close>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.DontShowAgain>Don't show these again</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Button.DontShowAgain>

  <!-- Spoken feedback. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.OpeningChangelog>Opening the changelog in your browser.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.OpeningChangelog>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.AllMarkedRead>All announcements marked as read.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.AllMarkedRead>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Suppressed>Okay. Future updates will give only a brief notice. You can turn these messages back on in Options, RimWorld Access.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Suppressed>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Closed>What's New closed.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.Closed>

  <!-- Brief notice spoken instead of the full reader when the player has turned auto-popups off.
       {0} is the newest version. -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.UpdateWhisper>RimWorld Access updated to version {0}. Open What's New from the menu to read what changed.</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.UpdateWhisper>

  <!-- Menu items (main menu and in-game pause menu). -->
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.MenuItem.WhatsNew>What's New</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.MenuItem.WhatsNew>
  <RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.MenuItem.Website>RimWorld Access website</RimWorldAccess.WhatsNew.MenuItem.Website>

</LanguageData>
